Streamlined the async telemetry path so the handlers pass `SearchTelemetryContext` directly into the metrics layer instead of unpacking attributes at each call site.

Changed:
- Added context-aware overloads in [SearchResponseMetrics.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G002_elasticsearch/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/rest/action/search/SearchResponseMetrics.java) for:
  - `recordTookTime(...)`
  - `incrementResponseCount(...)`
  - `recordSearchPhaseDuration(...)`
  - `recordStoreBytesRead(...)`
- Updated [AbstractSearchAsyncAction.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G002_elasticsearch/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/search/AbstractSearchAsyncAction.java) to record store bytes and phase duration using the telemetry bundle directly.
- Updated [TransportSearchAction.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G002_elasticsearch/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/search/TransportSearchAction.java) so `SearchTelemetryListener` records took time and response counts from the bundle directly.
- Updated [CanMatchPreFilterSearchPhase.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G002_elasticsearch/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/search/CanMatchPreFilterSearchPhase.java) to pass the bundle into phase-duration telemetry.
- Kept the bundle construction centralized in [SearchTelemetryContext.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G002_elasticsearch/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/search/SearchTelemetryContext.java).

Verification:
- `git diff --check` passes.
- I did not run Gradle tests in this checkout.

