parts.text:
Refactored the search REST parsing path to be flatter and easier to follow, without changing the external API.

What changed:
- Broke `parseSearchRequest` in [RestSearchAction.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G002_elasticsearch/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/rest/action/search/RestSearchAction.java) into smaller helpers for:
  - request-body parsing
  - request-parameter application
  - post-validation/tail handling
- Split `parseSearchSource` in the same file into focused helpers for query, windowing, field selection, tracking, sorting, stats, and suggestions.
- Simplified CCS round-trips handling in [SearchParamsParser.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G002_elasticsearch/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/rest/action/search/SearchParamsParser.java) and made the param name explicit via a constant.
- Added focused coverage in [SearchParamsParserTests.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G002_elasticsearch/server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/rest/action/search/SearchParamsParserTests.java) for:
  - non-CPS behavior
  - CPS defaulting
  - CPS warning emission when the param is explicitly set

Verification:
- `git diff --check` passed.
- I could not run Gradle tests in this checkout because `gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar` is missing, and there is no local `gradle` binary available.

If you want, I can next do the same kind of structural cleanup in another nearby REST action or search-related parser.

